  <!-- STORY -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="about-story">
        <p>When we started {{ site.name }} back in {{ site.founded }}, screen enclosures were already a staple of Florida life — but good ones weren't always easy to find. Permits getting skipped. Aluminum too light for the wind load. Screen installed without knowing the difference between 18×14 and 18×16. We built this company to do it right.</p>
        <p>Over twenty years later, we've built hundreds of pool enclosures, screen rooms, and porch enclosures across {{ site.areaServed }}. We've rescreened enclosures we didn't build, and we've rebuilt ones that weren't done correctly the first time. We've seen what fails after five years — and we don't build that way.</p>
        <p>Every job we take is permitted and inspected. That's not just a legal requirement — it protects you when you sell your home, file an insurance claim, or ride out a storm. We won't skip that step, and you shouldn't want us to.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

